00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.450
Abraham: There are many different
cyber security controls and there are

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.110
many different ways to apply them.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.800
The exact method used will depend
on the type of control and the

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.610
system it is being applied to.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.479
Some will be simple processes that
can be executed by the IT department,

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.869
but some will involve bringing
in specialists to implement them.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:22.070
Nicole: So, let’s look at some of
the controls we have already covered.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.350
Passwords, usernames and
multifactor authentication.

00:00:26.929 --> 00:00:30.110
To protect against the risk of
phishing attacks more secure

00:00:30.139 --> 00:00:34.230
passwords should be used and these
could be changed on a regular basis.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.630
Abraham: The introduction of multifactor
authentication can also reduce

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.349
the potential for phishing scams.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.560
If staff leave their passwords lying
around offering easy access to others

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.840
having multifactor authentication can
make the system, more secure by having

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.069
to add a code sent to a mobile device.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.570
If many employees are working
remotely then remote lock out

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:00.030
can be used if too many incorrect
guesses are made on passwords.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:04.720
Nicole: Having remote workers can
also have an impact, as remote VPNs

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.939
and WiFi connections are notoriously
vulnerable to malware and viruses.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:13.220
Antimalware can be readily installed
by just hitting an install button

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.460
and following instructions.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.260
Encrypting documents and storage
devices can also be done quite easily.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:22.900
Abraham: Limiting access to
files and folders can be done by

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.800
setting up a permissions policy.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.880
By limiting permission there is
less opportunity of inappropriate

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.010
access to data and information.

00:01:31.389 --> 00:01:34.630
Nicole: The first line of defence
in cyber security is regularly the

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:38.340
employees, as they can often literally
open the door to threat actors.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.530
Implementing periodic security
awareness training for all members of

00:01:42.539 --> 00:01:46.899
staff can help to keep the workforce
up to date with the threat landscape.

